The [`Plumber`] object has a method called [`open`]. When you call it from code
that the plumber does not run, the valve opens on the plumber's own thread and
the call returns a handle at once.

```rust
let plumber = Plumber::new();
let handle = plumber.open(Pipe::hot());
assert!(handle.is_open());
```

[`Plumber`]: https://docs.example.com/plumbing/2/plumbing/struct.Plumber.html
[`open`]: https://docs.example.com/plumbing/2/plumbing/struct.Plumber.html#method.open

Another way is to give the plumber a channel and let it send gauge readings back
to the caller, which then never touches a valve itself.

```rust
let (tx, rx) = plumbing::channel();
plumber.report_to(tx);
for reading in rx {
    println!("{reading}");
}
```
